## Performance Guidelines

### Memory Management

- Minimize object allocations in hot paths
- Use object pooling for frequently created objects if needed
- Prefer `dict` over objects for key-value lookups when keys are dynamic
- Reuse objects where safe (e.g., HTTP client sessions)

### Async/Await

- Use `async`/`await` for all I/O operations
- Use `asyncio.gather()` for parallel operations
- Use `asyncio.as_completed()` when you need results as they complete
- Handle cancellation with `asyncio.CancelledError`
- Use `asyncio.create_task()` for concurrent operations

### Caching

- Cache at the appropriate level (Entry, Group, or Project)
- Use sliding expiration for frequently accessed items
- Use absolute expiration for stable data
- Consider cache size limits (LRU eviction)
- Use `functools.lru_cache` for function-level caching when appropriate

